# Build context for the outfit-tagger image is cloud-webapp/outfit-tagger/
# (deploy-outfit-tagger.sh runs `gcloud builds submit $REPO_ROOT/outfit-tagger`),
# so cloud-webapp/.dockerignore does NOT apply here — Docker reads the
# .dockerignore at the context root. The Dockerfile copies `*.py` by glob (so new
# modules are never silently omitted); these excludes keep tests, caches, and
# local-only data out of the image.
**/test_*.py
**/conftest.py
**/requirements-test.txt
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/pytest-cache-files-*
**/.venv
local_store/
samples/
*.log
.DS_Store
